 ('dawn-provision','Dawn — selected paragraphs for the FDRG','Octavia E. Butler; excerpt hosted by SPACE','https://www.spacestudios.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/Dawn-by-Octavia-Butler-selected-paragraphs-for-the-FDRG.pdf','indexed_primary_excerpt','The living ship’s engineered structures supply food, oxygen, waste processing, transport and living space.','Only a short indexed selected passage was used, not the novel or a full PDF reconstruction; living technology is not automatically autonomous AI.'),
 ('dawn-scope',"Lilith’s Brood",'Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilith%27s_Brood','secondary_reference','Dawn’s awakened human captives/survivors, living Oankali ship, healing and imposed gene-trade framework.','Later Earth resisters, the proposed Mars colony and unawakened people are not this shipboard population.'),
